    <FieldNote
      title="The Pro Secret: Using an Angle Grader Flap Disc for Fast Copes"
      trade="Production Finish Carpentry"
      content="While a manual coping saw blade works wonderfully for small rooms, production trim carpenters rarely use hand saws on tall baseboard profiles. Mount an 80-grit flap sanding disc on a 4-1/2-inch variable-speed angle grinder. After making your 45-degree miter cut on the chop saw, use the spinning flap disc to effortlessly grind away the back-bevel wood right up to the pencil line in less than 15 seconds. It leaves a laser-clean edge without tearout."
    />
  </div>

